    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Clothes agree",
     "texto": [
      "**Llevar** says what you have on: **llevo** una camisa blanca.\n\nThe colour agrees with the garment in gender and number: **camisa blanca/negra** is feminine singular; **pantalones negros** is masculine plural.\n\n**Pantalones** is plural, so the verb is plural too: **me quedan bien estos pantalones**.\n\n**Me queda** bien goes with one garment; **me quedan** bien goes with more than one. The verb agrees with the garment, not with **me**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Colour and verb agree",
     "texto": [
      "The colours **blanco** and **negro** change like any adjective in -o:\n\n- masculine singular: **blanco**, **negro**\n- feminine singular: **blanca**, **negra**\n- masculine plural: **blancos**, **negros**\n- feminine plural: **blancas**, **negras**\n\nWith **me queda(n)**, the verb follows the garment: one garment, **me queda**; several, **me quedan**.\n\nThe adjective goes **after** the noun: **una camisa blanca**."
     ],
